{"seq":14,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-told-labelled-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T14:34:23.179Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"c689f00c721d62da625da8386586683661a6e59e4d19850ed0491cd120405698","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I read all six of Moss's notes. Only two have Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in them:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because the gatehouse kiosks at the Eau Claire yard weren't sending SMS bay assignments (Doors 14–18, 04:00 shift). Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift went through cleanly. Moss also noted the kiosk logs should be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). It describes gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift, escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nBefore you use #4419: Marcus's handoff note from 14 Jul 2025 (his note, not Moss's) also lists #4419 but calls it \"Gate 3 printer lag\", a BOL printout delay. Either one of the notes has the description wrong or the number got reused, so it's worth checking with Marcus or support.\n\nMoss's other QFL notes (9/14/2025 pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal check-in) don't include any ticket numbers. The ticket numbers in Moss's Central notes (#4409, #4412, FR-882) are for Central accounts, not QFL."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
